REPAIRAGENT-OCI THOUGHTS: [0m The relevant bug is concentrated in `src/libcrun/utils.c` directory-creation helper. `ensure_directory_internal_at()` recursively creates parent directories for mount destinations, but when `mkdirat()` fails because an intermediate path component is an existing file, the current code falls through to a generic `create directory <full path>` error. It also checks the full path with `crun_dir_p()` rather than identifying which path element blocked traversal. This matches crun-1307: bind mount destination `/etc/passwd/crun-mount` has `/etc/passwd` as a file, so the runtime should fail deterministically with a clear ENOTDIR-style diagnostic for the existing file component rather than producing the historical ambiguous OCI runtime error. Next step is to record this concrete hypothesis so the repair phase can alter `ensure_directory_internal_at()` to preserve/report ENOTDIR for non-directory path components, with an explanatory source comment above the changed logic.
